  "body": "The Post dialog now opens where this document last posted, proposing the same file, or beside the saved project as `<project name>.nc`. It used to open with no folder and `program.nc` every time.\n\n### What changed\n\n- New `crates/ui/src/post_file.rs`: `post_target(last_post, project)` is the rule, and `for_document(&State)` feeds it the G-code viewer's file (the last successful post) and `State::project_path`.\n  - Folder: the last post's, else the project's, else none (left to the OS).\n  - Name: the last post's file name, else `<project stem>.nc`, else `program.nc`.\n- `state.rs::post_program_dialog` takes that target: `set_directory` when there is a folder, and `set_file_name` from the target.\n- The remembered file is `PostView::path`, which New and Open already clear, so a new document never inherits another one's folder. A refused post writes nothing and doesn't move it.\n- One change from my claim on #258: the last post's name comes before the project's, so posting again after an edit proposes the file the shop already loads. The project name is the fallback for a document's first post. Reasons and dropped options (saving the folder in the project file) are in `docs/decisions/258-post-output-file.md`.\n\n### Tests (`post_file::tests`, ui lib)\n\n- `a_new_unsaved_document_proposes_program_nc_and_no_folder`\n- `a_saved_project_proposes_its_own_name_in_its_folder`\n- `the_last_post_sets_both_the_folder_and_the_name`\n- `a_documents_project_file_and_last_post_feed_the_dialog`: a real `State`, with the viewer's window closed.\n- `a_bare_file_name_opens_no_folder`\n- These test a new function, so there's no \"fails on main\" run. On `main` the dialog's arguments were the constants `program.nc` and no folder.\n\n### What ran (Windows 10, local, built from upstream `main` 8f30bee plus this commit)\n\n- The quick gate's plan for this diff (`scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -DryRun`, run by hand with `-j 4`): ui lib plus `boundary`, `boundary_picks`, `feedback`, `fixtures`, `gpu_render`, `machine`, `models`, `operations`, `shell`, and `theme_files` too. 368 pass, 2 ignored, 3 fail.\n- The 3 failures are the UI pixel snapshots (`egui_shell_snapshot`, `egui_shell_snapshot_light`, `tool_editor_snapshot`). They fail on clean `main` on this machine by the same pixel counts (1544, 1815, 2080; #255).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Not run: the native file dialog by hand (rfd can't run headless), Linux, macOS.\n\nChangelog: The Post dialog opens in the folder the document last posted to, with that file's name, or beside the saved project as <project name>.nc (#258)\n\nRefs #258\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
